      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nModelOpt Llama-4 checkpoints (for example, `nvidia/Llama-4-Scout-17B-16E-Instruct-FP8`) use fused expert weights. During weight loading, the sequence of `transpose`, `chunk`, and indexing operations produces non-contiguous CPU tensors. Copying non-contiguous tensors from CPU to GPU is significantly slower than copying contiguous tensors.\r\n\r\nThis change calls `.contiguous()` immediately before passing the tensor to `weight_loader`, ensuring efficient CPU-to-GPU transfers while preserving existing behavior. Since `.contiguous()` is a no-op for already contiguous tensors, this change is safe and has no functional impact.\r\n\r\nFixes #31624.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nNo new tests are required because this is a performance optimization with no behavioral changes.\r\n\r\n* Existing Llama-4 tests continue to verify correctness.\r\n* `.contiguous()` is a no-op for already contiguous tensors.\r\n* The change only ensures contiguous memory layout before GPU transfer.\r\n\r\n## Test Results\r\n\r\nNo functional tests were run for this change. The modification is limited to calling `.contiguous()` before `weight_loader` and does not alter the weight-loading logic or model behavior.\r\n\r\n## AI Assistance\r\nAI assistance was used in the implementation of this fix.",
